{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 9, :comments ["<b>And you shall take two shoham stones.</b> To atone for the two tablets that were shattered, and there the bundle came apart among these four — they are HaShem, blessed be He, and the tablets, and Moses, and Israel. And through the atonement all of them were joined together again, for the two shoham stones correspond to the two tablets. 'Shoham' — our Rabbi Bachya explained that it is the letters of the [divine] Name, and it is the letters of Moses (מֹשֶׁה — anagrammatically related to שֹׁהַם by letter permutation), and engraved upon it were all the names of the children of Israel. And from now on all four of them arrived at one inn together — whereas at first they forgot the El who saved them and caused that, correspondingly, HaShem forgot them too — behold, after the atonement they returned, ״וַיִּזְכְּרוּ כִּי אֱלֹהִים צוּרָם״ (Psalms 78:35), and then they too would be upon his two shoulders for a remembrance."], :book :exodus, :voice :kli-yakar, :lang :en, :chapter 28, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:23:49.533659495Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}